    "title": "pandas.tseries.offsets.Day.is_month_end — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1386.gcb2086a1a4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.tseries.offsets.Day.is_month_end#\n\n- \nDay.is_month_end(*ts* )#\n- Return boolean whether a timestamp occurs on the month end. This method checks if the given timestamp falls on the last day of a month, taking into account the frequency’s normalization settings. \n  - Parameters:\n    - **ts** Timestamp\n    - The timestamp to check.\n See also \n  - `is_month_start`\n  - Return boolean whether a timestamp occurs on the month start.\n Examples >>> ts = pd.Timestamp(2022, 1, 1) >>> freq = pd.offsets.Hour(5) >>> freq.is_month_end(ts) False",
    "markdown_length": 543,
